   200→  - _ulid: 01KF554T97ST9B3DMT4WMXACYQ
   201→    text: >-
   202→      Ralph Wiggum / Looper Mode - Create a kspec-integrated autonomous loop runner. Core idea: a
   203→      script that runs Claude Code repeatedly with fresh context, using a templated prompt that
   204→      instructs it to:
   205→
   206→
   207→      1. Run 'kspec session start' to see ready tasks
   208→
   209→      2. Pick a well-defined task (high priority, clear spec, no blockers)
   210→
   211→      3. Work on it until completion or stuck
   212→
   213→      4. Commit and complete the task
   214→
   215→      5. Exit cleanly (the outer loop restarts with fresh context)
   216→
   217→
   218→      Key features from research:
   219→
   220→      - Simple core: while :; do cat PROMPT.md | claude ; done
   221→
   222→      - Context persists via filesystem/git, not session memory
   223→
   224→      - Dual-condition exit: require both completion indicator AND explicit exit signal
   225→
   226→      - Circuit breaker: stop after N loops with no progress or repeated errors
   227→
   228→      - Rate limiting for API calls
   229→
   230→
   231→      Kspec-specific additions:
   232→
   233→      - Task selection heuristics (prioritize: clear AC, no blockers, isolated scope)
   234→
   235→      - Progress tracking via task notes before each exit
   236→
   237→      - Session checkpoint before exit to ensure clean state
   238→
   239→      - Maybe: task budget (only attempt tasks under estimated N turns)
   240→
   241→
   242→      The beauty is each iteration starts fresh but inherits cumulative work. Bad iterations don't
   243→      compound context - they just waste one run.
   244→    created_at: '2026-01-17T04:59:17.160Z'
   245→    tags:
   246→      - automation
   247→      - workflow
   248→      - agents
